; basics_stores.n — local stores pass their value through; shared stores consume.
; A local `x!` stores its value AND leaves it as an operand for the next op.
; A shared variable (declared by a top-level assignment) pops its value instead.
; Run: nk examples/basics_stores.n   → prints 6 4 5 9 (one per line)
0 total!                     ; top-level assignment declares the SHARED total
entry:
  5 3 sub d!                 ; d = 2 (local) — and the 2 stays on the stack
  d d mul                    ; leaves [2, 4]: the original 2 is still there
  add print                  ; 6 — the leftover 2 joined the addition
  5 3 sub d! d mul print     ; 4 — the correct square: the pass-through is the operand
  5 total!                   ; shared store CONSUMES the 5
  total print                ; 5
  total 4 add total!         ; 5 + 4 = 9, stored (consumed)
  total print                ; 9
  ret
